A Data Principal must:

* comply with all applicable laws while exercising her rights under the Act;  
* not impersonate another person when providing her personal data for a specified purpose;  
* not suppress any material information when providing her personal data for any document, unique identifier, proof of identity or proof of address issued by the State or its instrumentalities;  
* not register a false or frivolous grievance or complaint with a Data Fiduciary or the Board; and  
* furnish only information that is verifiably authentic while exercising the right to correction or erasure.  

[Section 15]
